  "text_md": "![](<54f9a795aa07178e6e31ac2baad40479bfde3aca_page_3_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nFig. 1. Antoni A: The tumor cells are irregularly arranged in cellular tissue fragment (Papanicolaou stain).\n\n![](<54f9a795aa07178e6e31ac2baad40479bfde3aca_page_3_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\nFig. 3. A fibrillary background substance contains cells with elongated nuclei with pointed ends (Diff-Quick stain).\n\n![](<54f9a795aa07178e6e31ac2baad40479bfde3aca_page_3_images/imageFile3.png>)\n\nFig. 2. Antoni B: Loosely cohesive and poorly cellular clusters of spindle cells are embedded in the fibrillar matrix (Papanicolaou stain).\n\n![](<54f9a795aa07178e6e31ac2baad40479bfde3aca_page_3_images/imageFile4.png>)\n\nFig. 4. The tumor cells show cohesive cells with indistinct cell border and round to oval nuclei. Variation of nuclear size and shape are seen (Papanicolaou stain).\n\n(Fig.\n\n",
